Package: akeR
Title: Compare Microbiome Distances Within and Between Groups
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Feargal", "Ryan", , "feargal.ryan@flinders.edu.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Calculates sample-to-sample distances from microbiome count
    data using compositional (Aitchison), abundance-based (Bray-Curtis,
    Hellinger, Jensen-Shannon and others), presence/absence and phylogenetic
    metrics, then compares them within and between groups with permutation
    tests that respect the non-independence of pairwise distances. Also
    measures the distance from each sample to a reference sample, such as a
    faecal microbiota transplantation donor or a subject's own baseline, and
    tests whether samples are closer to their own reference than to
    others.
